%% D3: one student message through the Turn API (apps/web/src/lib/play/v3/service.ts)
sequenceDiagram
  participant C as Student client
  participant API as Turn API<br/>(postAction)
  participant ENG as engine.step
  participant LLM as LLM provider
  participant DB as Postgres

  C->>API: POST /attempts/:id/actions {revision, message}
  API->>DB: loadAttempt, permittedAdventure
  Note over API: rate limit, revision check,<br/>token ceiling
  API->>ENG: step(spec, state, message)
  ENG->>LLM: character reply (replyAsCharacter)
  LLM-->>ENG: reply text
  ENG-->>API: state, events, view (pendingChecks queued)
  API->>DB: save state + append GameEvents (revision-guarded)
  API-->>C: 200 {revision, view, pendingCheckIds}

  Note over API,DB: after the response (Next.js after())
  Note over API: runPostTurnChecks<br/>(pendingCheckIds)
  API->>LLM: runPostTurnCheck: cheap structured call
  LLM-->>API: conveyed discoveries, challenged claims, moderation flag
  API->>ENG: step(spec, state, internal postTurn action)
  ENG-->>API: state, events (discovery, challenge, flag)
  API->>DB: save state + events + flags (revision-guarded, up to 3 tries)

  loop while view.pendingCheck
    C->>API: GET /attempts/:id (refresh with backoff)
    API-->>C: updated view (new notes)
  end
